Spec: Control authority verification host

Purpose:
  Own real server and Java child lifetimes while checking .NET control authorization.

Owns:
  ./ControlAuthority.Tests.csproj
  ./Program.cs

Structure:
  ./DataFixture.cs: Actual SDK data delivery, deterministic backend and scoped lifecycle.

Must:
  Hold verified source-built child processes in owned kill-on-close jobs and protect fixture directories.
  Never export client private keys, print raw error contents or let pending clients survive cleanup.
  Emit evidence only after all actual-network checks pass.
  Use uniquely named nonexportable per-user CNG test keys and delete their owned handles in final cleanup.
  Verify actual server epoch replacement and control outage close blocked data and preserve closed old guards.
  Verify an explicitly lagging client clock can acquire current authority using authenticated conservative response time without relaxing signed temporal claims.
